{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1127351-pooka-concepts-for-various-houses","id":1127351,"title":"Pooka concepts for various Houses?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-10T15:07:09-07:00","id":1127351,"title":"Pooka concepts for various Houses?","content":"So, a discussion from elsewhere started me pondering the fact that, in theory, a member of any Kith can end up a noble of any House. Which made me wonder, just what sort of Pooka would fit in with, say, Leanhaun or Dougal? And so I ask, what sort of character concepts do people have for Noble Pooka, especially ones from Houses that seem so &quot;un-Pooka-ish&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T15:28:30-07:00","id":1127365,"title":"","content":"Leanhaun make total sense for a pooka to me. Varich is the one that hurts my head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T08:23:11-07:00","id":1128053,"title":"","content":"Maybe not UNpookaish but I've had alot of fun with Pooka Ailil nobles... I've never quite gotten why people feel Pooka &quot;default&quot; to seelie. <br /> <br /> Other fun ones I had was a Eiluned mentor who basically played the role of mascot character in a magical girl game.....<br /> <br /> Aesin I feel needs an arcadian/Autumn break like Scathach have this is just a general issue with the house.<br /> <br /> Varich well 2e they were barely playable as for c20 I could easily see a Spider Pooka Varich...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T12:01:18-07:00","id":1128114,"title":"","content":"For Leanhaun, the most obvious always seemed a riff on the classic East Asian fox spirit (huli jing/kitsune/kumiho).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-16T12:38:27-07:00","id":1140890,"title":"","content":"A horse-pooka 'cavalryman' to House Gwydion. Sure, he irritates the s**t out of every other Gwydion in battle and he has a <i>really</i> morbid sense of humor, but, on the battlefield he is, pardon the pun, a <b>beast</b>. Primal Unleashing for the win!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-16T14:16:45-07:00","id":1140904,"title":"","content":"Owl Varich.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-16T15:24:05-07:00","id":1140911,"title":"","content":"Bat Pooka Ailil FTW. Winged, throw in some Slipped Seeming for permanent fangs, classy as heck.<br /> <br /> For a Dougal though... something tinkery. Rat, maybe? Raccoon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16912-fjordymcfjord","name":"FjordyMcFjord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16912_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-16T15:26:52-07:00","id":1140912,"title":"","content":"on Ailil Pooka? one problem, is one EXPECTS a pooka to lie.<br /> <br /> BAD for a member of house Ailil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-16T18:45:55-07:00","id":1140945,"title":"","content":"Even the devil tells the truth when it's to his advantage.<br /> <br /> Way back when, I had the concept of a Pooka commoner who was a leader of the local rebellion against the Nobles out in the West (Colorado, Wyoming and there a bouts). He was Boxer, the cunning old war horse, who was a master of guerrilla warfare and battlefield trickery who looked like a character right out of a John Wayne movie. (And yes, he's named after the horse from Animal Farm; the &quot;Boxer's Rebellion&quot; riff was an unintentional bonus.)<br /> <br /> I recently got to watch the anime Inu x Boku SS, and it struck me that the character of Miketsukami Soshi would make for a really good Fiona Pooka, being someone who has for all his life conformed his personality to please whomever he's around, literally living a lie, and only eventually finding his true self through his relationship with someone he's truly in love with. And to that end, he's completely unflappable and fearless, save when said love is threatened or distressed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-16T21:24:54-07:00","id":1140973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1127351-pooka-concepts-for-various-houses?p=1140912#post1140912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">on Ailil Pooka? one problem, is one EXPECTS a pooka to lie.<br /> <br /> BAD for a member of house Ailil.</div> </div> </div> </div>That could be the one pooka, who always tells the truth (and everyone, who doesn't believe it - suffers). <br /> <br /> Or, at least, the very best version of truth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-16T23:21:21-07:00","id":1140993,"title":"","content":"Everyone Expects Ailil to Lie. Whether someone believes something is less about the truth of the matter and their own fears and desires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T01:13:12-07:00","id":1141004,"title":"","content":"I actually did play an Ailil Bat Pooka for a while. Officially she was a diplomat, secretly she was in deep with the Shadow Court. She confused the hell out out of the local (Fiona) Countess at the time, as everything she said SEEMED like it must be true. There's way more to being a Pooka than saying the direct opposite of what is true. Exaggerations, understatements, deflections, feigned sarcasm, the list goes on...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16912-fjordymcfjord","name":"FjordyMcFjord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16912_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T06:35:49-07:00","id":1141044,"title":"","content":"I had a fox pooka Ailil npc in a chronicle I ran once. She was a master at using the image of the sweet, innocent pooka to manipulate members of the Seelie Court and uncovering their secrets.<br /> <br /> More recently, I had a peacock pooka ladies man npc I set up to be the rival of the Fiona sidhe pc (who fancied himself god's gift to women). The pooka wasn't a member of any house, but I always figured that if they ever got past their rivalry, they would have made a terrifying pair of Fiona fops. They never did.<br /> <br /> In the same chronicle, I had a raven pooka as the right hand of an extremely low ranking Ailil npc. It was a given that if the Ailil rose higher in her house, the pooka would ride her coat tails. That one was fun because the pc's decided that the raven pooka and their seelie sluagh friend npc would make the perfect couple. They spent a few entire game sessions trying to get the two npc's to hook up.<br /> <br /> I had a pooka fell rider of House Balor once, but that was a one off npc for a single session. Sadly, I can't remember that one's animal affinity anymore.<br /> <br /> A friend once played a cat pooka knight of House Liam for a few long running chronicles. I gave the character a cameo as an npc in a recent-ish chronicle I ran.<br /> <br /> For the C20 play test, I had a hedgehog pooka retainer for a House Eiluned noble. She ran the day to day upkeep of the freehold while his head was in the clouds studying the magical nature of glamour. It never came up in the games, but in my head the two were lovers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T07:01:55-07:00","id":1141055,"title":"","content":"When I run my next chronicle I intend to have an owl pooka librarian of House Aesin.<br /> <br /> In my first run of Immortal Eyes, one of my gamers had a koala pooka. Loved it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Krister M. Michl</b> <hr /><b>Freelance writer</b> <hr /><a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Krister_M._Michl\" target=\"_blank\">Entry on White Wolf Wikipedia</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2494-rigistrade","name":"Rigistrade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2494_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T10:47:49-07:00","id":1141462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rigistrade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1127351-pooka-concepts-for-various-houses?p=1141055#post1141055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I run my next chronicle I intend to have an owl pooka librarian of House Aesin.<br /> <br /> In my first run of Immortal Eyes, one of my gamers had a koala pooka. Loved it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aesin is one of my more favorite Houses. But if they were to have a signature Pooka member, he'd have to be a squirrel based on Ratatoskr, and be an incorrigible gossip who knows all the secret pathways through the Dreaming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T12:50:32-07:00","id":1141497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1127351-pooka-concepts-for-various-houses?p=1141462#post1141462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Aesin is one of my more favorite Houses. But if they were to have a signature Pooka member, he'd have to be a squirrel based on Ratatoskr, and be an incorrigible gossip who knows all the secret pathways through the Dreaming.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or a cow pooka, for the gigantic primordial heifer Ymir owned for a time.<br /> Or a dog pooka, for Wotan's Wild Hunt.<br /> Or an eagle pooka, for the eagle that nests in Yggdrasil's uppermost branches.<br /> Or a goat pooka, for the two goats that pulled Thor's chariot.<br /> Or a gorilla pooka for a jotun of particularly bestial descent.<br /> Or a horse pooka, for Sleipnir.<br /> Or a raven pooka, for either Hugin or Munin.<br /> Or a sea serpent pooka, for Jormundgandr.<br /> Or a snake pooka, for Nidhogg. <br /> Or a wolf pooka, for Fenris.<br /> <br /> Really, animals show up a lot in Norse myth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 09-18-2017, 06:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T13:00:01-07:00","id":1141505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1127351-pooka-concepts-for-various-houses?p=1141462#post1141462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Aesin is one of my more favorite Houses. But if they were to have a signature Pooka member, he'd have to be a squirrel based on Ratatoskr, and be an incorrigible gossip who knows all the secret pathways through the Dreaming.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of my issues with Aesin is i don't think it quite think the flaw meshes well with nonarcadian fae. I'm also not so sure about the Boon whatsoever...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T22:37:26-07:00","id":1141666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1127351-pooka-concepts-for-various-houses?p=1128053#post1128053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Other fun ones I had was a Eiluned mentor who basically played the role of mascot character in a magical girl game.....<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sooo something like this guy?<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/originals/94/85/8f/94858f05b76e5189a7ed446fc1d28d7d.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T23:28:59-07:00","id":1141672,"title":"","content":"That is definately how he'd see himself!<br /> <br /> the other players gave the character the nickname &quot;Kyuubey&quot; though...((&quot;Omitting important parts of the truth is my Kith frailty!&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T19:44:11-07:00","id":1142003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1127351-pooka-concepts-for-various-houses?p=1140973#post1140973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That could be the one pooka, who always tells the truth (and everyone, who doesn't believe it - suffers).<br /> <br /> Or, at least, the very best version of truth.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Exactly. If you delve into KB:Pooka you see more examples of pooka-ese besides lying. All of it is about deception. What better way to deceive people than to tell the truth when they expect you to lie? You'll tell them everything and they'll never believe you! That would actually be a fun concept to play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://imgbb.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://image.ibb.co/fzeOgQ/1172c70f3ff188688852c74c8145285c_original_2_4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> Visit my freehold for Changeling links, settings, art, and other goodies.<br /> <a href=\"https://theshepherdsfreehold.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The Shepherd's Freehold</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13648-shepherd","name":"Shepherd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}